The argv equality and resolved-executable assertions are in integration_shell_live_linux_test.go.
These were native fake harnesses, not paid model runs. The hostile shell rc homes were
created from scratch and contained aliases, a function, and native PATH impostors;
no credentials or provider config homes were copied.

An initial probe did not start any server: its long test-temp config path exceeded
sockaddr_un. The successful probe uses a short os.MkdirTemp home for fake shell rc
only, with cleanup registered on t.Cleanup.
